descartes-discourse-2.md:1: argue/answered: S5: answered no, which keeps descartes-discourse-2.logic.r2, to: Suppose "where truth is of difficult discovery it is much more likely to be found by one than by many" is true and "a plurality of suffrages is no guarantee of truth where it is at all of difficult discovery" is false. Is S5, "And, finally, although such be the ground of our opinions, I remarked that a plurality of suffrages is no guarantee of truth where it is at all of difficult discovery, as in such cases it is much more likely that it will be found by one than by many.", true then?
